  "text": "Board of Elections\nShare\nTranslate\nEnglish\nAfrikaans\nAlbanian\nArabic\nArmenian\nAzerbaijani\nBasque\nBelarusian\nBengali\nBosnian\nBulgarian\nCatalan\nCebuano\nChinese (Simplified)\nChinese (Traditional)\nCroatian\nCzech\nDanish\nDutch\nEsperanto\nEstonian\nFilipino\nFinnish\nFrench\nGalician\nGeorgian\nGerman\nGreek\nGujarati\nHaitian Creole\nHausa\nHebrew\nHindi\nHmong\nHungarian\nIcelandic\nIgbo\nIndonesian\nIrish\nItalian\nJapanese\nJavanese\nKannada\nKhmer\nKorean\nLao\nLatin\nLatvian\nLithuanian\nMacedonian\nMalay\nMaltese\nMaori\nMarathi\nMongolian\nNepali\nNorwegian\nPersian\nPolish\nPortuguese\nPunjabi\nRomanian\nRussian\nSerbian\nSlovak\nSlovenian\nSomali\nSpanish\nSwahili\nSwedish\nTamil\nTelugu\nThai\nTurkish\nUkrainian\nUrdu\nVietnamese\nWelsh\nYiddish\nYoruba\nZulu\nHome\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard of Commissioners\n2026 Commissioners Meeting Schedule\n2009 - 2019 Agendas\n2009 - 2019 Minutes\nAgendas and Minutes\nDocument Archive (1969-2010 Minutes)\nCounty Holidays\nSunshine List\nWatch the Commissioners Meeting Here\nPublic Notices\nPolk County Ordinances\nMeeting Procedures, Rules, and Decorum\nDepartments & Services\nDepartments A-E\nAgricultural Economic Development\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard of Elections\nBuilding Inspections\nCommunications/911\nCooperative Extension\nCounty Manager\nEconomic Development\nEMS\nEmergency Management\nDepartments F - R\nFinance\nFire Marshal\nGIS\nHealth and Human Services\nHealth Department\nHuman Resources\nInformation Technology\nLibrary\nLicense Plate Agency\nMaintenance\nPlanning\nPublic Information Officer\nRecreation\nRegister of Deeds\nDepartments S-Z\nSheriff's Office\nSocial Services\nSoil & Water Conservation\nSolid Waste\nTax Assessor and Collector\nThe Meeting Place/Senior Center\nTransportation\nTravel and Tourism\nVeterans Services\nYMCA\nBusiness Resources\nChamber of Commerce\nRequest for Bids, Proposals, & Qualifications\nGIS Services\nPolk Agribusiness\nPolk County Municipalities\nColumbus\nTryon\nSaluda\nPermits\nPlanning\nResidents & Visitors\nAbout Polk County\nThings to Do\nAppearance Commission\nBuilding Inspection Permit Lookup\nEmployees\nGIS\nGovDeals\nJob Openings\nMeetings\nOrdinances\nRoad Signs - Report Missing or Damaged\nCounty Holiday Schedule\nAdditional Resources\nVisitor Center\nPolkNCInfo\nHow Do I\nSearch\nRelated Pages\nVoter Registration\nNC State Board of Elections\nElectronic Absentee Portal\nPrintable Absentee Ballot Request\nSign up for BallotTrax - Track your Absentee Ballot\nPolk County Polling Locations\n2026 General Election UOCAVA Notice\nHome\nBoard Of Elections\nBoard of Elections\n2026 General Election information\nEarly Voting\nDownload Flyer\nOctober 15 - 31\nWeekdays: 8:00am - 7:30pm\nSaturdays 8:00am - 3:00pm\nNo Sundays\nLocation: 231 Ward St Columbus NC.\nElection Day: November 3rd\nAll precincts open 6:30am - 7:30 pm.\nYou must vote at you precinct location on election day. No voting at BOE office.\nSAMPLE BALLOTS\nSaluda, Coopers Gap, White Oak (US Cong. Dist. 11) (outside municipalities)\nTryon, Green Creek, Columbus 1 &2, White Oak (US Cong. Dist. 14) (outside municipalities)\nColumbus 1 & 2 (inside municipality)\nSaluda (inside municipality)\nTryon (inside municipality)\nNext Board of Elections Meetings:\nRegular meetings are held the first Thursday of every month at 4:00pm.\nNext meetings:\nOctober 6th, 13th, 20th, 27th, November 2nd -\nAbsentee meeting @ 5pm\nAgenda: approve absentees\nNovember 3rd Absentee Meeting - TBD\nApprove and tally absentee ballots\n@ Board of Elections Office\n231 Ward St. Columbus NC 28722\n30 Day Residency Notice:\nYou must be a resident of North Carolina and of Polk County at least 30 days prior to any Municipal, Primary, General Election or Presidential Election.\nVOTER REGISTRATION APPLICATION\nCampaign Finance Information\nwww.ncsbe.gov\nThe Polk County Board of Elections is committed to conducting fair, honest, impartial and efficient elections so that all qualified citizens in Polk County may exercise their right to vote. The Elections Office is responsible for conducting all elections in Polk County, including municipal, county, state, and federal elections, as well as special referenda.\nServices Include\n:\n-Maintain Voter Registration Records\n-Receive Candidate Filing for General Assembly and local candidates\n-Campaign Finance office for local candidates/committees\n-Provide for Remote Absentee Voting\n-Provide for Election Day Voting\n-Report Election Day Results to Public and Authorities\n-Evaluate and Improve Election Services\n-Provide Election Reports and Statistical Information\n-Provide Precinct Official Training and Educate Election Day Officials\nOther Community Services Include:\n-Provide voter and precinct information to public\n-Provide registration materials and advice for community registration drives\n-Visit community groups for voter/election education\nNC State Board of Elections Web site =\nhttp://www.ncsbe.gov/\nThe following are the Board Members for 2025-2027:\nChair Scott Woodworth, Member Dr. Warren Carson, Member Keith Holbert, Secretary Libbie Johnson, and Member Veronica Pace\nContact Information\nSTAFF CONTACTS\nCliff Marr\nDirector of Elections\n828-894-8181\nContact Me\nBoard of Elections Address\n(Physical and Mailing)\n231 Ward St\nColumbus, NC 28722\nPO Box 253\n8:30 am -5:00 PM Mon-Fri\n828-894-8181\nContact Us\nShare\nthis page\nShare this page\n\u00d7\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.polknc.gov/board_of_elections_2.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nPlease ensure Javascript is enabled for purposes of\nwebsite accessibility\nContact\nInfo Site Map\nEmployment\nAgendas & Minutes\nHome\nEmployee Webmail\nBryant H. Womack Building\n40 Courthouse Street\nPO Box 308\nColumbus, NC 28722\nPHONE: (828) 894-3301\nMonday Through Friday\n8:30 A.M. To 5:00 P.M.\n\u00a9 2025 Polk County, NC | Powered by\nrevize.\n, the Government Website Experts. |\nLogin\nClose\nRead More",
